{
  "info": {
    "name": "Crumb & Co. — Backend API",
    "description": "Complete Postman collection for the Crumb & Co. e-commerce backend (Express v5 + Prisma).\n\n## Setup\n1. Start the server: `npm run dev` (defaults to http://localhost:4000).\n2. Seed the database: `npm run db:seed` (creates the admin `admin@crumbco.dev` / `Admin123!`, categories and products).\n3. Import the environment `crumb-and-co.environment.json` and select it.\n\n## How to run\n- Run the whole collection in order (Auth → Me → Users → Categories → Products → Cart → Orders → Cleanup).\n- Tokens are captured automatically: Login requests store the JWT in the collection variable `accessToken` / `adminAccessToken`, which every protected request reads.\n- Refresh tokens are httpOnly cookies handled automatically by Postman's cookie jar.\n- Re-running is mostly idempotent: create requests tolerate 409 (already exists). If an earlier create 409s, later requests reuse the seeded category/product captured from the list endpoints.\n\n## Auth model\n- Register/login → access JWT (Bearer). Refresh token delivered via httpOnly cookie on `/api/v1/auth`.\n- Admin endpoints require the seeded admin (or any user promoted via PATCH /users/:id/role).\n- Mock payment provider auto-marks orders PAID.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminAccessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "customerUserId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "managedUserId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "categoryId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "productId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "createdProductId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "orderId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "Register, login, refresh, logout. Tokens are saved to collection variables for downstream requests.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register Customer",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{customerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{customerPassword}}\",\n  \"name\": \"Jane Doe\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 on first run (409 if email already registered)', () => pm.expect([201, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.test('returns created user', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.email).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register Managed User",
          "description": "Second account used by the admin-management tests in the Users folder.",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"managed@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Managed1!\",\n  \"name\": \"Managed User\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 on first run (409 if already registered)', () => pm.expect([201, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('managedUserId', pm.response.json().data.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login Customer",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{customerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{customerPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('success is true', () => pm.expect(json.success).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.test('returns accessToken', () => pm.expect(json.data.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.data.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('customerUserId', json.data.user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login Admin",
          "description": "Uses the seeded admin (see `npm run db:seed`).",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns accessToken', () => pm.expect(json.data.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminAccessToken', json.data.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh",
          "description": "Reads the httpOnly `refreshToken` cookie automatically. Rotates the session and returns a fresh access token.",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('rotates accessToken', () => pm.expect(json.data.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.data.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 204', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', '');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — invalid payload (400)",
          "description": "Shows the real validation error shape: `details` is an array of {field, message}.",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"not-an-email\",\n  \"password\": \"short\",\n  \"name\": \"\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('code is VALIDATION_ERROR', () => pm.expect(json.error.code).to.eql('VALIDATION_ERROR'));",
                  "pm.test('details is an array of {field, message}', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json.error.details).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.error.details[0]).to.have.property('field');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.error.details[0]).to.have.property('message');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Me",
      "description": "Current authenticated user (customer token).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Me",
          "auth": {
            "type": "bearer",
            "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
          },
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns current user', () => pm.expect(json.data).to.have.property('email'));",
                  "pm.test('email matches logged-in user', () => pm.expect(json.data.email).to.eql(pm.environment.get('customerEmail')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Me",
          "auth": {
            "type": "bearer",
            "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
          },
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Jane Q. Doe\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('name updated', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.name).to.eql('Jane Q. Doe'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
